[ ] Lint the minimal CLI profile in CI =lint-minimal $Found 2026-10-06: cargo build --release -p clearhead --no-default-features warns dead_code, and CI lints only default features, so the minimal profile drifts unseen. Add a clippy step with --no-default-features (-D warnings), then fix what it finds.$ !4 ^2026-10-06T10:41 #01a1124e-2a1c-74fe-ae3e-14f6701598ca
[ ] Test the CLI on Windows in CI =windows-ci $Run the test suite on a windows-latest CI runner, including atomic replace while an editor holds the file. Once it passes, add x86_64-pc-windows-msvc as a target in dist-workspace.toml.$ !4 ^2026-10-06T15:09 #01a11343-bb68-7361-9d1c-75244453feb0
[ ] Keep line endings when formatting .actions =keep-line-endings $Add a clearhead-cli test in tests/actions.rs checking that format turns CRLF input into LF. Land it together with the specifications pin bump to formatting 3.2.0.$ !4 ^2026-10-06T15:09 #01a11343-bb79-749d-938c-8989d16bab59
[ ] One changelog format\: Keep a Changelog =changelog-format $Put every entry under its version (Unreleased, renamed at release) so parse-changelog can extract it. Convert the specification and CLI changelogs, add one to clearhead.nvim, bring Core past 0.1.0, and move the CLI Roadmap to a charter if it is still live.$ !4 ^2026-10-06T15:50 #01a11369-8cb1-731d-acdd-02ac93a2e67d
[ ] Assemble clearhead-core's root changelog =core-root-changelog $A script assembles the root CHANGELOG.md from Core's and the CLI's, committed because dist reads its release notes only from a real root file; CI regenerates it and fails on a difference. Then regenerate the v0.3.0 release notes, which shipped with none.$ !4 ^2026-10-06T15:50 <changelog-format #01a11369-8cc5-7639-91fe-4ba6541b1cea
[ ] Release the platform as a set of pinned components =platform-release $A platform release tags the platform repository whose gitlinks are component releases; proposed CalVer (2026.10.0), since the bundle has no single notion of breaking. Its changelog is assembled per release: for each component whose pin moved, that component's sections between the old and new versions, read from git.$ !5 ^2026-10-06T15:50 <core-root-changelog #01a11369-8cd7-76c0-83fa-6fd49112f05b
[ ] Trim the runbook to platform rules now that agent-sandbox delivers run-kind contracts =runbook-dedupe $Remove the generic rules from docs/overnight-runbook.md that agent-sandbox's run-kind contracts now cover (=review-contract) and point there instead. Keep the platform-only rules: scripts/gate.sh, clearhead CLI use, dependency gate, provenance and Stopping.$ !3 ^2026-10-13T05:20 #01a137e5-f743-7242-baa0-6583fcaca3da
[ ] Ship a VS Code extension that runs clearhead-lsp for .actions files =vscode-extension $In its own repo, ClearHeadToDo-Devs/clearhead.vscode (a submodule here), build a thin language client that launches clearhead-lsp, then a TextMate grammar. Needs the Windows binary, so windows-ci comes first. It proves itself on fixtures and a doctor check.$ ^2026-10-16T21:33 <core-habit-ship #01a146a2-9238-7591-98fe-5bb1ac22fdce
[ ] Publish clearhead 0.4.0 to crates.io =core-0-4-crates $NEEDS TOKEN: this host has no crates.io credentials. From clearhead-core at tag v0.4.0, run cargo publish -p clearhead_core, then cargo publish -p clearhead. Or decide the registry can wait and cancel this.$ !3 +human ^2026-11-05T01:49 #01a1a965-9658-75e1-99f8-3ab2f9ea79d5
